WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.546 --> 00:00:06.631
With what's going on in our society,

00:00:06.631 --> 00:00:10.510
with women and the autonomy of their bodies,

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:12.929
it's important that art reflects life.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:15.432
It's an honor to get to explore this story

00:00:15.432 --> 00:00:18.935
because I know hard conversations have to be had 

00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:21.146
surrounding missing women

00:00:21.146 --> 00:00:23.690
and human trafficking.

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:26.985
You don't hear about it.
You don't read about it.

00:00:26.985 --> 00:00:30.488
The rape, murder, and trafficking 
of black and brown girls

00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:33.783
has never been anyone's priority,

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:35.285
ever, in any capacity.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:40.415
Gabrielle, she is an advocate
for survivors of sexual trauma.

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:44.169
She's very outspoken about 
her own past with sexual trauma.

00:00:44.294 --> 00:00:46.755
And I think she really relied on

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:48.465
the strength and the pain

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.383
that she's had to grapple with.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:53.928
My story is pretty well known.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.764
I've been talking about it 
for the last 25 years.

00:00:55.972 --> 00:01:00.685
I was raped and beaten 
at 19 in the Bay Area.

00:01:00.894 --> 00:01:03.146
A lot of the locations are very familiar.

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.231
A lot of the situations are very familiar.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:08.276
I've had 30 years to intimately understand

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:10.153
sexual violence against black and brown girls

00:01:10.153 --> 00:01:11.738
and how we are...

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:13.239
systemically ignored

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.867
and blamed for our own trauma.

00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:19.454
She brought a grit and a fire.

00:01:19.496 --> 00:01:20.622
She's brilliant.

00:01:20.622 --> 00:01:22.624
But I know it also cost her.

00:01:23.166 --> 00:01:26.503
You are doing a lot of good in this world.

00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:28.004
Well I want to do more.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:32.884
I need to do more.

00:01:32.884 --> 00:01:35.386
The thing about trauma is it's not linear.

00:01:36.054 --> 00:01:38.264
And surviving and healing is not linear.

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:40.558
We really pull back the curtain on 

00:01:40.558 --> 00:01:43.186
how a girl becomes groomed,

00:01:43.186 --> 00:01:44.687
how she's trafficked,

00:01:44.687 --> 00:01:45.772
and the aftermath.

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:47.357
The attempts to reclaim your life.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:52.862
Season three is so full of deep heartbreak, 

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:53.988
courage,

00:01:53.988 --> 00:01:55.615
and also triumph of the human spirit.

00:01:56.533 --> 00:01:59.369
It's looking at the 
juxtaposition between

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:01.663
the way the police, the media, and the government 

00:02:01.663 --> 00:02:04.374
respond to young white women,

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:06.251
and the way they respond
to minority groups.

00:02:06.251 --> 00:02:08.211
The fact that they are being left behind.

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:10.880
It's really tied to something happening in Oakland,

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:13.216
happening in our country, and in our world.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:14.926
Where we can highlight an issue

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:16.719
that people were not talking about,

00:02:16.719 --> 00:02:17.971
that they really should be.

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.849
We need you to put pressure 
on the police department

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:22.934
to bring these girls home.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:26.020
They're real circumstances
that people are living every day.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:29.315
And if we can shine
a light on this subject,

00:02:29.399 --> 00:02:32.110
maybe we can save a life.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.696
It's taken me 30 years to unpack.

00:02:34.696 --> 00:02:35.780
And through this show,

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.574
 and hopefully through me and my history,

00:02:37.574 --> 00:02:39.868
we can give it the large platform

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.619
and the attention it deserves.

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.705
It feels like we are fighting
for our very breath,

00:02:43.705 --> 00:02:44.706
our very life.

00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:47.375
Because there's legit women,

00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:48.626
and girls, and boys

00:02:48.626 --> 00:02:50.086
hanging in the balance.

00:02:50.378 --> 00:02:51.296
It's that important.

00:02:51.296 --> 00:02:52.338
The work that we're doing,

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.549
season three is that important.

00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.593
And everyone understood the assignment.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.262
My name is Poppy Scoville, 

00:02:59.262 --> 00:03:02.265
and I need you to reconsider.

00:03:02.473 --> 00:03:04.517
You have no idea what that little thing

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.561
can mean to a survivor.

